I have a feeling some people will cringe at this but.. Harry Potter. 
Even though it's mainly targeted at children, plenty of adults have read 
them too and I think it's safe to say that after 6 books and 4 movie 
adaptations, all successfuly, it's more than a fad. (Lasting appeal is 
important.)

And of course, it's loaded with magical creatures and items.

Gillyweed - A food item gives amphibiousness temporarily.Can be found 
growing in the water, may turn up elsewhere rarely. Technically you 
should lose the ability the breath air for the duration, but that would 
probably make it too hard to use. A warning as it's expiring (unless 
cursed?) would be in order I think.

Avada Kedavra - Killing Curse. Pretty much like the Finger of Death. 
Some reference to it assoiciated with that spell might be amusing.

Mandrake - Used to cure petrification in the HP world, but there are 
probably enough ways to do that already.

Protego (Shield Charm) - A spell offering temporary reflection.

Dementor - Particularly nasty W. Drains levels and/or thoughts (like a 
mind flayer, exenpt no INT loss).

Foe-Glass - Special mirror that shows the owners enemy. The clearer the 
image closers the enemy. Could just be monster detection, but I think it 
would be cooler if it only focused more a the big bad guys, but detected 
them accross levels. Could also warn id Rodney's impending return from 
the dead.

Marauder's Map - Artifact scroll. Invoke for Magic Mapping plus monster 
detection. Would be reusable, of course.

Seven-Lock Trunk - Basically a chest of holding. Not too useful I guess, 
it seems like it has potential though.

Time Turner - Uh.. No nevermind.

I'm sure someone could think of more.

